      "source": [
        "# Intrusion Detection Pipeline\n",
        "Using the autoencoder and OpenAis o4-mini model, we finally create a full flow through. It looks like the following:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Get raw original dataset\n",
        "2. Clean the dataset using a modified cleaning function\n",
        "3. Load pretrained autoencoder\n",
        "4. Inference the dataset\n",
        "5. Get all anomalous packets and link them back to the original raw dataset\n",
        "6. Extract statistics from surrounding packets\n",
        "7. Feed all information in o4-mini LLM\n",
        "8. Get final explaination, LLM-based risk score\n",
        "\n",
        "This code only runs the AE model and LLM model for the smart grid dataset. It then shows an LLM output for each attack type. This is where we observe whether the LLM can perform good reasoning to determine the attacks and risk score.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Note from Jaxson: The LLM uses my money, please don't run too much!**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
